        {
          "say": "So the quotient is x plus 4, with no remainder.",
          "write": "(x + 3)(x + 4) = x² + 7x + 12"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The long division routine",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Does McDonald’s Sell Burgers? Divide, multiply, subtract, bring down.",
          "write": "D  M  S  B"
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide the front term by x. Write it on top.",
          "write": "x³ ÷ x = x²"
        },
        {
          "say": "Multiply the whole divisor by that term.",
          "write": "x²(x − 2) = x³ − 2x²"
        },
        {
          "say": "Subtract. Change every sign, then add.",
          "write": "2x² − (−2x²) = 4x²"
        },
        {
          "say": "Bring down the next term, and repeat."
        },
        {
          "say": "Stop when what is left has a lower power than the divisor."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "A full division",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Divide x cubed plus two x squared take five x take six by x take 2.",
          "write": "x³ + 2x² − 5x − 6",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y10/maths/dividing-polynomials-long.svg",
          "alt": "Long division of x cubed + 2x squared - 5x - 6 by x - 2"
        },
        {
          "say": "x squared, then four x, then 3 go on top.",
          "write": "Q = x² + 4x + 3"
        },
        {
          "say": "The last subtraction leaves zero.",
          "write": "R = 0"
        },
        {
          "say": "A remainder of zero means x take 2 is a factor.",
          "write": "(x − 2) is a factor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Placeholders and remainders",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Divide two x cubed take three x squared plus 4 by x plus 1.",
          "write": "2x³ − 3x² + 4"
        },
        {
          "say": "There is no x term. Write zero x to save its seat.",
          "write": "2x³ − 3x² + 0x + 4"
        },
        {
          "say": "Work through the routine. The last step is 4 take 5.",
          "write": "4 − 5 = −1",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y10/maths/dividing-polynomials-remainder.svg",
          "alt": "Long division of 2x cubed - 3x squared + 0x + 4 by x + 1 with remainder -1"
        },
        {
          "say": "So the quotient is two x squared take five x plus 5. Remainder minus 1.",
          "write": "(x + 1)(2x² − 5x + 5) − 1"
        },
        {
          "say": "Check with x equals 0. Both sides give 4.",
          "write": "x = 0: 4 = 5 − 1 ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Fraction form",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Divide x cubed take four x plus 7 by x take 3.",
          "write": "x³ + 0x² − 4x + 7"
        },
        {
          "say": "The quotient is x squared plus three x plus 5. The remainder is 22.",
          "write": "Q = x² + 3x + 5,  R = 22"
        },
        {
          "say": "The remainder goes over the divisor.",
          "write": "x² + 3x + 5 + 22/(x − 3)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Always write zero placeholders for missing powers."
        },
        {
          "say": "Subtract every term. Minus two x squared becomes plus two x squared."
        },
        {
          "say": "Do not stop while there is still an x term left."
        },
        {
          "say": "Write the remainder over the divisor, not on its own.",
          "write": "✗ Q(x) + 22"
        }
      ]
    },
